[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837370018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837370018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837370018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kuZ6i","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T20:38:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T20:38:58Z","body":">Joints without a gizmo surface cannot be selected\r\n\r\nI'm mixed on this, I understand that's how it worked in v4.5, but technically it is part of the transform gizmo and an argument can be made that it should also have priority over the bone buttons, especially since there is a dedicated select tool now. What if someone wants to use the trackball feature to manipulate the joints?\r\n \r\n>The rotation gizmo does not function in Transform mode\r\n\r\nHuh weird, I can make it work sometimes. I'll take a further look.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837370018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837390818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837390818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837390818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kue_i","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T20:46:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T20:49:29Z","body":"> What if someone wants to use the trackball feature to manipulate the joints?\r\n\r\nThis operation must be performed when you press a part inside the sphere that does not exist as a joint button. It is selectable in 4.6 stable, but this PR is causing further regressions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837390818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837408065","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837408065","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837408065,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kujNB","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T20:53:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T20:53:52Z","body":">This operation must be performed when you press a part inside the sphere that does not exist as a joint button.\r\n\r\nIsn't that the issue that this PR is trying to fix? IMO the transform gizmo should consistently have priority over the bone buttons.\r\n\r\nWouldn't it make sense more to have the trackball an editor setting if this is considered an issue for people who preferred the behavior of being able to select through the gizmo while it's transform/rotation mode? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837408065/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837416736","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837416736","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837416736,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kulUg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T20:57:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:02:23Z","body":"Since you might be confused, let me clarify the issue. The issue points out that the joint button takes precedence over the green (XZ) plane transform in the video.\r\n\r\n4.6:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85f2c129-40c1-4fd7-8f40-557ade0c9379\r\n\r\n4.5:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2dacdaf9-0719-41f9-a025-44dd1bab0396\r\n\r\nThis PR currently treats everything inside the sphere as part of the transform gizmo's detection, but that's the wrong approach. The only necessary fix here is to ensure that items visually positioned higher take priority when clicked.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837416736/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837466929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837466929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837466929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kuxkx","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T21:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:17:00Z","body":">Since you might be confused,\r\n\r\nThis is certainty possible. 😂\r\n\r\n>The issue points out that the joint button takes precedence over the green (XZ) plane transform in the video.\r\n\r\nI believe I understand this.\r\n\r\n>This PR currently treats everything inside the sphere as part of the transform gizmo's detection, but that's the wrong approach.\r\n\r\nYes, and I am arguing that the approach makes sense. It is part of the transform gizmo and therefore should have priority over the bone buttons as well. This will lead to consistent behavior and makes it impossible to accidentally select a different bone if someone was rapidly trying to rotate the track ball.\r\n\r\nMy alternative suggestion is we make it an editor setting to disable the trackball for those who prefer not to use the dedicated select tool and wish to click through the transform/rotation gizmo. \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837466929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837514646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837514646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837514646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ku9OW","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T21:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T22:07:01Z","body":"> Yes, and I am arguing that the approach makes sense. It is part of the transform gizmo and therefore should have priority over the bone buttons as well. This will lead to consistent behavior and makes it impossible to accidentally select a different bone if someone was rapidly trying to rotate the track ball.\r\n\r\nThat must be a separate proposal.\r\n\r\nThe author who reported the issue apparently hasn't touched anything other than 4.6, so I don't know if they want that, but I'm simply arguing that we need to preserve the 4.5 behavior, so we should only make \"fixes\" here, not enhancement.\r\n\r\nAs I said initially, whether to add an option to enforce that transform gizmo area requires discussion and demand assessment through a proposal. Personally, I wouldn't strongly oppose it, but it should never be the default (it means that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114749 will recur within Sphere), and I wouldn't promote that adding it (I'll leave that to others' opinion who want to it).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837514646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837771865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115608#issuecomment-3837771865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115608","id":3837771865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kv8BZ","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravata